
This project contains a dataset and analysis of the Danish royal lineage (Kongerækken),
created as part of the Digital Methods course assignment. The project focuses on 
structuring historical data and applying basic analytical methods in R.
The dataset was manually compiled (Excel) and transformed into a format (CSV) suitible
for analysis, and the results are documented in the .html and .rmd files.

The data is based on the offical Danish royal lineage published by the Danish Royal 
House: https://www.kongehuset.dk/monarkiet-i-danmark/kongerakken 

The Danish monarch lineage was manually structured into an Excel file, where the 
relevant variables iclude:
  Monarch name
  Year of birth
  Year of death
  Start of Reign
  End of Reign
Afterwards, the dataset was exported from .xlsx to .csv for use in R

In the Week_11 folder you can find the following:
  Danish_Monarchs.csv - clean dataset used in analysis
  DanishMonarchs.rmd - R Markdown file with code and explanations
  DanishMonarchs.html - Rendered output of the analysis

Author: Johanne Ø. Daugbjerg
